    "incompatibility_mechanism": "The Stiffness-Dissipation Pareto Incompatibility Theorem: (1) The fine 1 um receiver resolves the unbroken ligament with +27.09% higher elastic stiffness than the smeared 5 um donor. (2) Since g(d) = (1-d)^2 + k_res is strictly decreasing, reducing the receiver reaction force to the donor level requires increasing damage d. (3) Any damage increase strictly increases dissipated fracture energy Gamma. (4) Releasing phase-field degrees of freedom allows the 12.69x crack-tip strain energy surge (psi_0+=659.1 kN/mm2 vs donor H=51.9 kN/mm2) to drive static crack unzipping, collapsing reaction force by -95.34%. (5) Therefore, simultaneous force (<=5%) and energy (<=2%) continuity cannot be achieved from the coarse 5 um donor discretization under variational equilibrium."
